# KiCad: always reopen PCB after updates

**Mandatory last step of the turn** — do not wait for the user to ask.

Whenever this turn **changes or regenerates** the ESP32 baseboard PCB / schematic
(`pcb/esp32_baseboard/esp32_baseboard.kicad_pcb`, `.kicad_sch`, `gen_power_carrier.py`
output, footprints under `pcb/esp32_baseboard/libraries/`), **before finishing the
user-facing answer**:

1. Finish generator / file edits first.
2. **Kill** existing KiCad / pcbnew processes for a clean reload.
3. **Start-Process** KiCad (or pcbnew) with the PCB file so the user sees the new board.

Do this at the **end of every such answer** so the user never stares at a stale PCB window.

## Paths

- PCB: `d:\Project\coutingmachine\pcb\esp32_baseboard\esp32_baseboard.kicad_pcb`
- Prefer opening the `.kicad_pcb` with **pcbnew.exe** (layout editor).
- Exe on this machine:  
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\KiCad\10.0\bin\pcbnew.exe`  
  (also `kicad.exe` in the same folder; version folder may be `9.0` / `10.0`)

## PowerShell

```powershell
$pcb = "d:\Project\coutingmachine\pcb\esp32_baseboard\esp32_baseboard.kicad_pcb"
Get-Process -Name kicad,pcbnew,KiCad -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
$kicad = @(
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\KiCad\10.0\bin\pcbnew.exe",
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\KiCad\10.0\bin\kicad.exe",
  "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\KiCad\9.0\bin\pcbnew.exe",
  "${env:ProgramFiles}\KiCad\9.0\bin\pcbnew.exe"
) | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
if (-not $kicad) { throw "KiCad exe not found" }
Start-Process -FilePath $kicad -ArgumentList "`"$pcb`""
```

## When it does NOT apply

- Pure docs / git / non-PCB work with no `esp32_baseboard` layout change
- User explicitly says not to reopen KiCad
